# A widget read as a blueprint value in a method call's argument
# (`loud.?Pick(@One)`, the call `?Pick loud, @One` written as a method; Semantics ch. 8: a
# blueprint is a value, and a function may take one). Given as a plain call's argument
# the same lowers (sem-ch08-blueprint-value-gives-back). `ValueWidgetsIn` looks at a
# call's arguments, not a method call's. Reaches `WidgetNamed`'s refusal "the widget function
# @One as a value" on prismc-fd1.
# Written by Claude (sweep-7, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@One: @unit
@One:
    Ui.Label($text=$"one")

?Pick: fn Bool, @a -> ?@a
fn ?Pick b, @w = if b: ? @w else: nil

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    match loud.?Pick(@One):                                           # 0
        ? @t: @t
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"none")
